    {
      "game": "Assassin’s Creed Valhalla",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/6147/450x258/assassin-s-creed-valhalla-pc-game-ubisoft-connect-europe-cover.jpg?v=1791172800",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/6147-buy-assassin-s-creed-valhalla-pc-game-ubisoft-connect-europe/",
      "user": "ja robot",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "Valhalla is a very disappointing game because it had so much potential. The biggest problem is that it is way too long and has a lot of filler content that makes the game feel repetitive. There are also way too many in-game purchases for a full-priced game.\n\n\n\nThe characters and story are also very forgettable. After only two months, I barely remember any of the characters, which is disappointing for such a huge game.\n\n\n\nOn the positive side, the gameplay is really fun, the combat feels great, and the game is absolutely beautiful. Norway is especially stunning—almost every screenshot there could be a wallpaper. I also enjoyed the modern-day story. I just wish we could equip two bows at once.\n\n\n\nOverall, Valhalla is a beautiful and fun game, but its length, filler, monetization, and forgettable story stop it from reaching its full potential."
    },
